Hardware Watchdog arms the watchdog timer in the host's chipset with
watchdogd, so a host that stops working is reset by its own hardware
instead of waiting for somebody to pull the power. It is disarmed at
every shutdown. On AMD processors of family 17h or later it also reads,
at every boot, why the host last reset, as the chipset recorded it.

Where os-xgs-npu already arms the timer, this plugin leaves it to it and
only shows it.

